            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The petitioners argue that door\u2011to\u2011door solicitation without first obtaining a village permit is a criminal act."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Polidoro (Petitioner)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "59d8591f9a3dc92d965e0c54afa094ac5a2d844c2e761a81a4cb95aeae6eb7b9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-59d8591f9a3d-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 19,
              "start": 19
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Polidoro (Petitioner), the petitioners also contend that, after historic battles in the 1930s\u20111940s, municipalities have stopped trying to regulate Jehovah\u2019s Witnesses by requiring such permits."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Cantor (Respondent)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "59d8591f9a3dc92d965e0c54afa094ac5a2d844c2e761a81a4cb95aeae6eb7b9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-59d8591f9a3d-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 31,
              "start": 31
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Cantor (Respondent), the respondents maintain that the village\u2019s purpose in requiring a permit is to prevent annoyance to property owners."
      }
    ],
